[0m⚙ [0mcompress {"topic":"Ellipse Cutouts Review Analysis","content":[{"startId":"m0001","endId":"m0006","summary":"TASK: Independent code review of the 'ellipse-cutouts' feature branch in the Roblox classic-clothing editor (Preact/TypeScript/Canvas2D/Three.js, mobile-first, for ages 8-10). User instruction: \"Follow the complete review instructions in the first attached file.\" Output format required: findings as `SEVERITY (BLOCKER|IMPORTANT|MINOR) - file:line - concrete failure - specific fix`, then EXACTLY one verdict line: `VERDICT: APPROVE` / `APPROVE WITH CHANGES` / `REJECT`. Omit praise, summaries, style preferences, speculation, scope expansion. State unverifiable gaps rather than guessing.\n\nSETTLED CONSTRAINTS (from review prompt reviews/ellipse-cutouts-review-prompt.md): Add has one Cut Out entry then Rectangle/Oval choices; dragging defines bounding rect, tapping Oval makes a circle; both shapes reuse move/4 side handles/proportional corner scaling/rotation/wheel scaling/visibility/copy/undo-redo/More; Cut Outs erase alpha via Canvas2D destination-out after all paint on the canonical canvas used by export/2D/3D; strict schema v3 requires shape: 'rectangle'|'ellipse', v1 migrates directly to v3, v2 cutouts become rectangles preserving name/geometry; old names preserved, new names 'Rectangle Cut Out N'/'Oval Cut Out N'; max 8 layers, no accounts/cloud, offline must work; Color/Cutout More sheets must have NO nested scroll at 844x390 (raster More intentionally scrollable); Roblox Studio calibration is a separate manual gate. Verification is claimed green: typecheck/lint/223 unit/178 browser/build/bundle/PWA/12 Playwright E2E across Chromium+Firefox+WebKit.\n\nEVIDENCE FILES READ AND ANALYZED (all under .worktrees/ellipse-cutouts): reviews/ellipse-cutouts-branch.diff (full), docs/2026-09-01-ellipse-cutouts-design.md, docs/2026-09-01-ellipse-cutouts-implementation-plan.md, src/project/archive.ts, src/editor/state.ts, src/editor/ui/{designer-app.tsx, editor-screen.tsx (via diff), workspace.tsx, gestures.ts, sheets.tsx, icons.tsx, preview-pane.tsx}, src/compositor/compose.ts, src/project/export.ts.\n\nVERIFIED-IMPLEMENTATION FACTS (with file:line):\n- types.ts: CutoutShape='rectangle'|'ellipse'; CutoutLayerV2 extends LayerBase {kind:'cutout';rect}; CutoutLayer extends CutoutLayerV2 {shape}; ProjectDocumentV2 (schemaVersion 2) added; ProjectDocument schemaVersion 3; Layer=PaintLayer|CutoutLayer.\n- state.ts: CUTOUT_KEYS_V2 = {id,name,kind,visible,rect}; CUTOUT_KEYS_V3 adds 'shape'. isValidCutoutLayerShape (state.ts:229) requires hasOnlyKeys V3 + shape in {rectangle,ellipse} + hasValidCutoutBase. hasValidDocumentHeader accepts 1|2|3 (state.ts:270). isValidProjectDocumentV1 (297) paint-only; isValidProjectDocumentV2 (327) validates v2 cutouts + paint-before-cutout ordering + dup-id + raster asset refs; isValidProjectDocument (364) requires schema 3 + valid shape. migrateProjectDocumentV1 (323) → schemaVersion 3 (paint-only copy). migrateProjectDocumentV2 (353) maps cutouts to {..., shape:'rectangle', rect:{...}} preserving name/id/visibility/geometry. ItemSpec cutout now {kind:'cutout';shape;rect}. addItem (656) names `${item.shape==='ellipse'?'Oval':'Rectangle'} Cut Out ${next.cutout}`; duplicateItem (720) names from source.shape. LayerCounters.cutout is monotonic (not restored on undo/redo — intentional, pre-existing).\n- archive.ts openProject (235-244): branches schemaVersion===1→isValidV1+migrateV1; ===2→isValidV2+migrateV2; ===3→isValidProjectDocument; else invalid. Save validates isValidProjectDocument first (117).\n- compose.ts validateDocument (57-73) now rejects cutout shape not rectangle/ellipse; eraseCutout (292-310) translate/rotate then branch: ellipse → beginPath+ctx.ellipse(0,0,w/2,h/2,0,0,2π)+fill; else fillRect(-w/2,-h/2,w,h). globalCompositeOperation='destination-out', globalAlpha=1, fillStyle='#000000'.\n- gestures.ts: pointInFootprint (92-114) inverse-rotates point by -rotationDeg and for ellipse tests (rx/halfWidth)^2+(ry/halfHeight)^2 <= 1+1e-6, else axis-aligned bounds. cutoutRect (284-315) tap path: width=max(32,size.width*0.25), height=max(32,size.height*0.2); if ellipse diameter=min(w,h) then w=h=diameter (circle). hitLayerId passes layer.shape for cutouts (325). Handles (rotate/scale/edge) tested BEFORE interior hit in startItemInteraction (343-424). onWheel/onKeyDown also pass shape (814, 892). onPointerDown cutout path (659-677) sets cutoutDraw with shape; onPointerMove/Up guard `!drawingCutout?.() || cutoutShape?.()!==cutoutDraw.shape` (694, 723) clearing cutoutDraw+draft on mismatch.\n- workspace.tsx: strokeEllipse (142-159) and strokePolygon for selection outlines; overlay dataset.draftShape/selectionShape set truthfully (240-295); draft stroked as ellipse vs strokeRect (250-256). cutoutFootprint uses footprintGeometry with scaleX/Y=1 and rect w/h. Props changed drawingCutout:boolean → drawingCutoutShape:CutoutShape|null.\n- designer-app.tsx: drawingCutoutShape state (118); resetTransient sets setDrawingCutoutShape(null) (236) and is called in startGarment/runNewProject/goStartScreen/onOpenFile. onChooseCutoutShape (759-768) checks item cap then setSheet('cutout-shape'). onStartCutout(shape) (770) setSheet(null)+setActiveTab('edit')+setDrawingCutoutShape(shape). onCreateCutout(rect,shape) (776-793) guards `drawingCutoutShape!==shape` and item cap, dispatches add-item, clears drawingCutoutShape. onToolbar (590) and onTabChange (854) clear drawingCutoutShape.\n- sheets.tsx: CutoutShapeSheet (103-134) with SheetBackdrop label 'Cut Out Shape', two big-choice buttons aria-label Rectangle/Oval with IconRectangle/IconOval + visible span, sheet-cancel. MoreSheet compact flag (539) = layer.kind==='cutout' || (solid && placement==='decal'); applies sheetClass 'compact-more-sheet'. isDecalSolid (393).\n- icons.tsx: strokeIcon helper (3); IconRectangle=['M4 6h16v12H4z']; IconOval manual svg ellipse rx9 ry6.\n- export.ts uses composeProject (57); preview-pane.tsx uses composeProject (81); workspace.tsx uses composeProject (209). So 2D/3D/export/save all share the canonical canvas — no mismatch path found.\n- styles.css: .compact-more-sheet .more-form {flex:0 0 auto; overflow-y:visible}; .compact-more-sheet .field {flex-direction:row}; .compact-more-sheet .field input {width:5rem}. Base `.more-sheet .more-form{overflow-y:auto}` remains for raster.\n- Tests updated: compose.test.ts ellipse corner-preservation+rotated+union; export.test.ts ellipse alpha at center + opaque corner (300,290); gestures.test.ts pointInFootprint ellipse/rotation + harness corner-ignore test; ui.test.ts shape chooser + Escape/backdrop/Cancel + one Add entry; archive.test.ts v1→v3, v3 deterministic roundtrip, v2→rectangle migration preserving data, strict unknown-shape/missing-shape/hybrid rejection; editor-state.test.ts Oval naming + shared monotonic counter; mobile-layout.spec.ts compact More no-overflow assertion at 844x390 + oval touch drag.\n\nFINDINGS CONFIRMED FOR THE REVIEW:\nF1 (IMPORTANT): gestures.ts:762-767 onPointerCancel for cutoutDraw clears cutoutDraw + onCutoutDraft(null,null) but does NOT clear the chosen shape (drawingCutoutShape). The gesture controller options have no cancel-cutout callback (Workspace never wires onCancelCutout into the controller). Design doc line 88 (docs/2026-09-01-ellipse-cutouts-design.md 'Geometry and gestures') explicitly states pointer cancellation clears BOTH the draft AND chosen shape. Consequence: after a pointercancel during draw, draw mode stays active (instruction bar + Cancel remain visible), draft cleared, no layer created (benign, no data corruption), but contradicts the settled design and is UNTESTED (no test exercises the cutoutDraw branch of onPointerCancel). Fix: add an onCancelCutout callback to GestureControllerOptions, wire Workspace→props.onCancelCutout, and call it in onPointerCancel when cutoutDraw was active; or explicitly document the deviation.\nF2 (MINOR): gestures.ts:660-662 onPointerDown cutout branch early-returns `if (cutoutDraw !== null) return;` without re-validating drawingCutout()/cutoutShape(). In a contrived multitouch sequence (Escape/tab-change mid-drag clears drawingCutoutShape, then re-enter draw mode and issue a second pointerdown before the original pointerup is delivered), the new pointerdown is silently dropped because stale cutoutDraw is still non-null. Move/Up handlers DO clear via the drawingCutout()/cutoutShape() guard, so it self-heals on pointerup. Fix: mirror the mismatch guard in onPointerDown (if cutoutShape() !== stored shape, reset cutoutDraw before starting).\n\nNO BLOCKER FOUND. All schema/migration paths, ellipse pixel erasure, shape-aware hit-testing, tap-circle diameter, handle priority, naming, item-cap, undo/redo, save/open, export, preview, and 844x390 compact-More overflow are correctly implemented and test-covered. Minor cosmetic note (not a reported finding): compose.ts:70 mislabels unknown-shape as 'invalid cutout geometry' message."}]}
